{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1466 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "7a77947db0168a32b9f7b26c2c3c30926cf618c9ebd3ac5a14ea808310f98dc5" :edb/db-before-t 1465 :edb/db-after-t 1466 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534778 50 #inst "2026-10-08T06:38:58.407Z" 13194139534778 true] [17592186087523 1100 "The velocity vector $\\mathbf{v} = \\langle u, v \\rangle$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = \\langle 12t+t^2, t^3+1\\rangle.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $\\mathbf{a}$." 13194139534778 true] [17592186087523 1100 "The velocity vector $\\mathbf{v} = \\langle u, v \\rangle$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n$\\mathbf{v} = \\langle 12t+t^2, t^3+1\\rangle$.\nCalculate the acceleration vector $\\mathbf{a}$." 13194139534778 false] [17592186087523 1145 "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na &= \\frac{dv}{dt} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{du}{dt}, \\frac{dv}{dt}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{d}{dt}(12t + t^{2}), \\frac{d}{dt}(t^{3} + 1)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨12 + 2t, 3t^{2}⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534778 false] [17592186087523 1145 "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(12t+{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12+2t,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534778 true] [17592186087524 1100 "The position vector $\\mathbf{r}$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 4t^2+1, 3t^2-t\\rangle.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $\\mathbf{a}$." 13194139534778 true] [17592186087524 1100 "The position vector $\\mathbf{r}$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n$\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 4t^2+1, 3t^2-t\\rangle$.\nCalculate the acceleration vector $\\mathbf{a}$." 13194139534778 false] [17592186087524 1145 "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector. We can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv &= \\frac{dr}{dt} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{dx}{dt}, \\frac{dy}{dt}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{d}{dt}(4t^{2} + 1), \\frac{d}{dt}(3t^{2} - t)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨8t, 6t - 1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na &= \\frac{dv}{dt} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{du}{dt}, \\frac{dv}{dt}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{d}{dt}(8t), \\frac{d}{dt}(6t - 1)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨8, 6⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534778 false] [17592186087524 1145 "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector. We can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2}+1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8t,\\,6t-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6t-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534778 true] [17592186087559 1100 "The velocity vector $\\mathbf{v} = \\langle u, v \\rangle$, measured in $\\textrm{m}/\\textrm s$, of a particle $P$ at time $t$ seconds, is given by\n$\\mathbf{v} = \\langle t^4-t^2, 2t^3\\rangle$.\nFind the acceleration vector and the magnitude of the acceleration of $P$ at time $t=1$." 13194139534778 false] [17592186087559 1100 "The velocity vector $\\mathbf{v} = \\langle u, v \\rangle,$ measured in $\\textrm{m}/\\textrm s,$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ seconds, is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = \\langle t^4-t^2, 2t^3\\rangle.\n$$\n\nFind the acceleration vector and the magnitude of the acceleration of $P$ at time $t=1.$" 13194139534778 true] [17592186087559 1145 "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na &= \\frac{dv}{dt} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{du}{dt}, \\frac{dv}{dt}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{d}{dt}(t^{4} - t^{2}), \\frac{d}{dt}(2t^{3})⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨4t^{3} - 2t, 6t^{2}⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=1$, we substitute $t=1$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na(1) &= ⟨4(1)^{3} - 2(1), 6(1)^{2}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨2, 6⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $\\mid \\mathbf a(1) \\mid$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}a(1) & &= & ⟨2, 6⟩\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{2^{2} + 6^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{40} \\\\\n&= 2\\sqrt{10}m/s^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534778 false] [17592186087559 1145 "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4{t}^{3}-2t,\\,6{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=1,$ we substitute $t=1$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(1) & =⟨4(1)^{3}-2(1),6(1)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|\\mathbf a(1)|\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(1)| & =|⟨2,6⟩| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{40} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534778 true] [17592186087560 1100 "The position vector $\\mathbf{r}$, in meters, of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ seconds is given by\n$\\mathbf{r} = \\left\\langle t^{5}-t^2,\\, t^2+6t-3 \\right\\rangle$.\nCalculate the acceleration vector and the magnitude of the acceleration of $P$ at time $t=0$." 13194139534778 false] [17592186087560 1100 "The position vector $\\mathbf{r},$ in meters, of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ seconds is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\left\\langle t^{5}-t^2,\\, t^2+6t-3 \\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector and the magnitude of the acceleration of $P$ at time $t=0.$" 13194139534778 true] [17592186087560 1145 "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv &= \\frac{dr}{dt} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{dx}{dt}, \\frac{dy}{dt}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{d}{dt}(t^{5} - t^{2}), \\frac{d}{dt}(t^{2} + 6t - 3)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨5t^{4} - 2t, 2t + 6⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na &= \\frac{dv}{dt} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{du}{dt}, \\frac{dv}{dt}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{d}{dt}(5t^{4} - 2t), \\frac{d}{dt}(2t + 6)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨20t^{3} - 2, 2⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=0$, we substitute $t=0$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na(0) &= ⟨20(0)^{3} - 2, 2⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 2, 2⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $\\mid \\mathbf a(0) \\mid$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}a(0) & &= & ⟨ - 2, 2⟩\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(-2)^{2} + 2^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{8} \\\\\n&= 2\\sqrt{2}m/s^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534778 false] [17592186087560 1145 "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{5}-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+6t-3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5{t}^{4}-2t,\\,2t+6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5{t}^{4}-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t+6)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨20{t}^{3}-2,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=0,$ we substitute $t=0$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(0) & =⟨20(0)^{3}-2,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|\\mathbf a(0)|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(0)| & =|⟨-2,\\,2⟩| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534778 true] [17592186087702 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309632 13194139534778 true] [17592186087702 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309637 13194139534778 true] [17592186087702 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309643 13194139534778 true] [17592186087702 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309690 13194139534778 true] [17592186087703 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309618 13194139534778 true] [17592186087703 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309656 13194139534778 true] [17592186087703 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309661 13194139534778 true] [17592186087703 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309666 13194139534778 true] [17592186087703 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309697 13194139534778 true] [17592186087737 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309597 13194139534778 true] [17592186087737 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309604 13194139534778 true] [17592186087737 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309611 13194139534778 true] [17592186087737 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309648 13194139534778 true] [17592186087737 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309653 13194139534778 true] [17592186087738 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309625 13194139534778 true] [17592186087738 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309671 13194139534778 true] [17592186087738 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309676 13194139534778 true] [17592186087738 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309681 13194139534778 true] [17592186087738 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309686 13194139534778 true] [17592186088228 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534778 true] [17592186088228 1100 "The velocity vector $v = ⟨u, v⟩$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$v = ⟨5t - 8, 2t^{2} + 4⟩$.\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a$." 13194139534778 false] [17592186088228 1100 "The velocity vector $v=⟨u,v⟩$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nv=⟨5t-8,\\,2{t}^{2}+4⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a.$" 13194139534778 true] [17592186088228 1145 "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5t-8),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2}+4)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309597 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309598 13194139534778 true] [17592186309597 1089 "q-121917" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309597 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534778 true] [17592186309597 1100 "The velocity vector $v=⟨u,v⟩,$ measured in $\\text{m}/\\text{s},$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ seconds is given by\n\n$$\nv=⟨-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩.\n$$\n\nFind the magnitude of the acceleration of $P$ at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{8}.$" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309597 1113 #uuid "accdf36e-4deb-5652-9073-b1834a2b81f8" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309597 1145 "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{8},$ we substitute $t=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =⟨4\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}),2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|a(\\frac{\\pi }{8})|:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(\\frac{\\pi }{8})| & =|⟨4,2⟩| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309598 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309599 13194139534778 true] [17592186309598 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309600 13194139534778 true] [17592186309598 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309601 13194139534778 true] [17592186309598 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309602 13194139534778 true] [17592186309598 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309603 13194139534778 true] [17592186309598 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534778 true] [17592186309598 1041 "selection" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309598 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309602 13194139534778 true] [17592186309598 1110 #uuid "fcc9b4f8-afc5-5ccc-9705-b13c094ffb66" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309599 1034 "2\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309599 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534778 true] [17592186309599 1111 #uuid "c0c87bb3-4a1e-5eee-8571-dbb4ddb80169" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309600 1034 "\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309600 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534778 true] [17592186309600 1111 #uuid "2577bf1f-28c9-55aa-9795-bd89ae4067d5" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309601 1034 "5\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" 13194139534778 true] [1