te the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({2}^{t-1}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{2}^{t-1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,-\\frac{2t}{({t}^{2}+1)^{2}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=1,$ we substitute $t=1$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(1) & =⟨{2}^{1-1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,-\\frac{2(1)}{({1}^{2}+1)^{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{2}^{0}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,-\\frac{2}{4}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,-\\frac{1}{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|a(1)|:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(1)| & =|⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,-\\frac{1}{2}⟩| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{ln}^{2}⁡2+\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{4{ln}^{2}⁡2+1}{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{4{ln}^{2}⁡2+1}}{2}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309613 13194139534778 true] [17592186309612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309614 13194139534778 true] [17592186309612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309615 13194139534778 true] [17592186309612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309616 13194139534778 true] [17592186309612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309617 13194139534778 true] [17592186309612 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534778 true] [17592186309612 1041 "selection" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309612 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309614 13194139534778 true] [17592186309612 1110 #uuid "7e63b100-734c-59f9-90da-29f98ac4158f" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309613 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2{ln}^{2}⁡2+1}}{4}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309613 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534778 true] [17592186309613 1111 #uuid "4de9a797-f1ce-5b26-95ae-b407bc40c871" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309614 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{4{ln}^{2}⁡2+1}}{2}\\,{\\text{m