ents of the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t.$\n\n$a=⟨${{field-1}},{{field-2}}$⟩$" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309643 1113 #uuid "32aed3df-fecd-5116-8366-f0c14f8d968a" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309643 1145 "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({2}^{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+1))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}+1}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309644 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309645 13194139534778 true] [17592186309644 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534778 true] [17592186309644 1041 "field-1" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309644 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309645 13194139534778 true] [17592186309644 1110 #uuid "37164766-c4cf-59f7-b1b4-3d979594054d" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309645 1034 "2^t\\ln(2)" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309645 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534778 true] [17592186309645 1111 #uuid "2974d91c-0100-55cd-b6ab-7d141f5084f4" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309646 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309647 13194139534778 true] [17592186309646 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534778 true] [17592186309646 1041 "field-2" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309646 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309647 13194139534778 true] [17592186309646 1110 #uuid "dbb809df-90a5-50b6-9c7b-c93a541ffe49" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309647 1034 "\\frac{2t}{t^2+1}" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309647 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534778 true] [17592186309647 1111 #uuid "46a81839-4d09-5cd5-8e94-6d6e516beac2" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309648 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309649 13194139534778 true] [17592186309648 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309651 13194139534778 true] [17592186309648 1089 "q-351167" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309648 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534778 true] [17592186309648 1100 "The velocity vector $v=⟨u,v⟩$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nv=⟨4{t}^{3},\\,-2{t}^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the components of the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t=1.$ Do not round the answers.\n\n$a(1)=⟨${{field-1}},{{field-2}}$⟩$" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309648 1113 #uuid "6114abe5-977b-5d52-bf38-29f0303c45f9" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309648 1145 "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12{t}^{2},\\,-4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the acceleration at time $t=1,$ we substitute $t=1$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(1) & =⟨12(1)^{2},\\,-4(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12,\\,-4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12,\\,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309649 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309650 13194139534778 true] [17592186309649 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534778 true] [17592186309649 1041 "field-1" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309649 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309650 13194139534778 true] [17592186309649 1110 #uuid "f8ab3c75-8fb1-5d76-9bce-4222c94b8a3d" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309650 1034 "12" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309650 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534778 true] [17592186309650 1111 #uuid "20cd8292-d4c3-58b2-ab94-2e6e7ae19a90" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309651 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309652 13194139534778 true] [17592186309651 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534778 true] [17592186309651 1041 "field-2" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309651 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309652 13194139534778 true] [17592186309651 1110 #uuid "44625857-1179-57b4-a112-ca1dc2ffc089" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309652 1034 "-4" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309652 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534778 true] [17592186309652 1111 #uuid "3fc3a10c-3e7d-5deb-993f-48d3fe1fbc32" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309653 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309654 13194139534778 true] [17592186309653 1089 "q-351176" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309653 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534778 true] [17592186309653 1100 "The velocity vector $v=⟨u,v⟩,$ measured in $\\text{m}/\\text{s},$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ seconds is given by\n\n$$\nv=⟨3{t}^{2}+2t-1,-4t+5⟩.\n$$\n\nFind the magnitude of the acceleration of $P$ at time $t=1\\,\\text{s}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe magnitude of the acceleration is\n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309653 1113 #uuid "ea008953-1c5b-5269-bd0d-c70f8fe25f40" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309653 1145 "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}+2t-1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-4t+5)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6t+2,\\,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=1,$ we substitute $t=1$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(1) & =⟨6(1)+2,-4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|a(1)|:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(1)| & =|⟨8,-4⟩| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{80} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the magnitude of the acceleration at time $t=1\\,\\text{s}$ is $4\\sqrt{5}{\\text{ m/s}}^{2}.$" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309654 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309655 13194139534778 true] [17592186309654 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534778 true] [17592186309654 1041 "field-1" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309654 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309655 13194139534778 true] [17592186309654 1110 #uuid "60418005-c94f-5ad6-90c0-f55fc85a1e6a" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309655 1034 "4\\sqrt{5}" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309655 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534778 true] [17592186309655 1111 #uuid "078f4a55-e197-5669-a3b5-12e60c824551" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309656 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309657 13194139534778 true] [17592186309656 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309659 13194139534778 true] [17592186309656 1089 "q-351377" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309656 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534778 true] [17592186309656 1100 "The position vector $r(t)$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{t}^{3}-4{t}^{2},\\,2{t}^{4}-{t}^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the components of the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t.$\n\n$a=⟨${{field-1}},{{field-2}}$⟩$" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309656 1113 #uuid "5acf3591-12db-5ea5-8cfd-578b4845491c" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309656 1145 "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-4{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{4}-{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2}-8t,\\,8{t}^{3}-2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-8t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8{t}^{3}-2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6t-8,\\,24{t}^{2}-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309657 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309658 13194139534778 true] [17592186309657 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534778 true] [17592186309657 1041 "field-1" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309657 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309658 13194139534778 true] [17592186309657 1110 #uuid "47fe4d9b-596a-5bff-b6fe-56e1c63319d9" 13194139534778 true] [175921863096