186309685 13194139534778 true] [17592186309684 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534778 true] [17592186309684 1041 "field-2" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309684 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309685 13194139534778 true] [17592186309684 1110 #uuid "63ad7b18-a753-5a43-a654-8e6b12ec1f74" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309685 1034 "10" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309685 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534778 true] [17592186309685 1111 #uuid "b5070a62-3897-50da-a2a3-c9829cf8ca0e" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309686 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309687 13194139534778 true] [17592186309686 1089 "q-351410" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309686 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534778 true] [17592186309686 1100 "The position vector $r,$ in meters, of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ seconds is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨3{t}^{3}-4{t}^{2}+2,\\,2{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}+5⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the magnitude of the acceleration of $P$ at time $t=1\\,\\text{s}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe magnitude of the acceleration is\n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{m/s}}^{2}$" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309686 1113 #uuid "ea9ca4c4-0c65-56db-9cd7-d20e345623e9" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309686 1145 "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{3}-4{t}^{2}+2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}+5)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9{t}^{2}-8t,\\,6{t}^{2}-2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(9{t}^{2}-8t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{2}-2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨18t-8,\\,12t-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=1,$ we substitute $t=1$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(1) & =⟨18(1)-8,\\,12(1)-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨18-8,\\,12-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨10,\\,10⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|a(1)|:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(1)| & =|⟨10,\\,10⟩| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{10}^{2}+{10}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100+100} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{200} \\\\  & =10\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the magnitude of the acceleration at time $t=1\\,\\text{s}$ is $10\\sqrt{2}{\\text{ m/s}}^{2}.$" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309687 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309688 13194139534778 true] [17592186309687 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309689 13194139534778 true] [17592186309687 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534778 true] [17592186309687 1041 "field-1" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309687 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309689 13194139534778 true] [17592186309687 1110 #uuid "db488ef3-c7b6-5436-b8ee-6d4b05be4b17" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309688 1034 "20" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309688 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534778 true] [17592186309688 1111 #uuid "7579ec8e-c23b-5e8e-954f-727f33689202" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309689 1034 "10\\sqrt{2}" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309689 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534778 true] [17592186309689 1111 #uuid "3e40f78e-d5d7-5f43-b127-269bbd39ebb8" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309690 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309691 13194139534778 true] [17592186309690 1089 "q-6393" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309690 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534778 true] [17592186309690 1100 "The velocity vector $v=⟨u,v⟩$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nv=⟨4{t}^{2},\\,-\\frac{3}{32}{t}^{4}⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a.$" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309690 1113 #uuid "1c5f639c-8e4f-5266-a543-d56a9c0dc420" 13194139534778 true] [17592186309690 1145 "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$